  "chunk": "maintain a coherent state across long sequences of actions, recalling which puz-\nzles they have solved, which items they have collected, and how different objects\n2\nmight interact. Moreover, the game provides sparse feedback through text re-\nsponses, requiring players to learn from both successes and failures to refine\ntheir understanding of the game world’s rules and logic.\nWhat makesZorkparticularly relevant for testing LLMs is how it depends\non distinctly human cognitive capacities. Human players leverage imagination\nto construct mental representations from textual descriptions, apply common-\nsense world knowledge to reason about object properties and causal relationships\n(understanding, for instance, that a lantern provides light, or that a sword can\nkill someone), and should continuously reflect on their own strategies, i.e., show\nsome level of metacognition. As Montfort [25] states in his analysis of interactive",
